WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:03.490
Oh, I see.

00:03.750 --> 00:06.870
In space, astronauts float because they're in freefall, like

00:06.890 --> 00:09.870
a gentle drop through space, so gravity pulls them, but

00:09.890 --> 00:11.510
they're not touching anything to feel it.

00:11.930 --> 00:14.930
It's like being in a falling elevator where everything floats together.

00:15.550 --> 00:18.210
So yes, gravity is there, but they feel weightless because

00:18.230 --> 00:19.230
they're falling freely.

00:19.360 --> 00:21.840
Once upon a time there was a little rabbit named Pip who

00:21.860 --> 00:24.180
couldn't fall asleep because the world was too bright and busy.

00:24.700 --> 00:26.580
So he climbed up to the tallest hill and looked down at the

00:26.600 --> 00:29.120
friendly moon who gently blinked and said, it's okay Pip just

00:29.140 --> 00:30.720
breathe one slow breath at a time.

00:31.200 --> 00:33.280
The moon shimmered softly and with each breath the stars

00:33.300 --> 00:34.940
twinkled like tiny lanterns.

00:35.380 --> 00:37.640
Soon Pip felt warm and calm and he whispered good night moon

00:37.660 --> 00:41.040
and closed his eyes dreaming of soft bunnies and dandelion fluff.

00:44.360 --> 00:46.400
Okay, here's your silly robot joke.

00:47.440 --> 00:49.220
I asked my robot, do you like cookies?

00:50.280 --> 00:52.420
It said, only if I get a power up.

00:52.940 --> 00:55.740
Then I gave it a cookie and it charged with joy.
